NUM-01: skip the link API pollutant flux when the link holds and receives no water

findLinkQual() and findSFLinkQual() convert the API link mass flux to a
concentration with flux * tStep / (v1 + qIn * tStep). For a dry conduit with
no inflow (v1 = 0, qIn = 0) the default zero flux gives 0/0 = NaN, which is
stored as the link's concentration and added to its load total and to the
External Inflow, Exfiltration Loss and Final Stored Mass terms of the quality
mass balance. Apply the flux only when it is non-zero and there is water to
carry it. A zero flux added nothing before, so wet links are unchanged.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply NUM-01_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/qualrout.c b/src/legacy/engine/qualrout.c
index 1cf5ae1..3e47df1 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/qualrout.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/qualrout.c
@@ -374,7 +374,9 @@ void findLinkQual(int i, double tStep)
         // --- Calculate bounded externally provided api pollutant flux and update mass balance
         cOut = Link[i].apiExtQualMassFlux[p];
 
-        if (cOut < 0.0)
+        // --- a link with no water (v1 + qIn*tStep = 0) takes no flux
+        //     (the division below would give 0/0 = NaN)
+        if (cOut < 0.0 && v1 + qIn * tStep > 0.0)
         {
             cOut = -cOut * tStep / (v1 + qIn * tStep);
             cOut = MIN(c2, MAX(0.0, cOut));
@@ -386,7 +388,7 @@ void findLinkQual(int i, double tStep)
             cOut = cOut/ tStep;
             massbal_addOutflowQual(p, cOut, FALSE);
         }
-        else
+        else if (cOut > 0.0 && v1 + qIn * tStep > 0.0)
         {
             cOut = cOut * tStep / (v1 + qIn * tStep);
             c2 += cOut;
@@ -450,7 +452,9 @@ void findSFLinkQual(int i, double qSeep, double fEvap, double tStep)
 
         cOut = Link[j].apiExtQualMassFlux[p];
 
-        if (cOut < 0.0)
+        // --- a link with no water (v1 + qIn*tStep = 0) takes no flux
+        //     (the division below would give 0/0 = NaN)
+        if (cOut < 0.0 && v1 + qIn * tStep > 0.0)
         {
             cOut = -cOut * tStep / (v1 + qIn * tStep);
             cOut = MIN(c2, MAX(0.0, cOut));
@@ -462,7 +466,7 @@ void findSFLinkQual(int i, double qSeep, double fEvap, double tStep)
             cOut = cOut/ tStep;
             massbal_addOutflowQual(p, cOut, FALSE);
         }
-        else
+        else if (cOut > 0.0 && v1 + qIn * tStep > 0.0)
         {
             cOut = cOut * tStep / (v1 + qIn * tStep);
             c2 += cOut;
